{"lines":[{"t":"Test 4","w":0.060194174448649093,"h":0.014650799997870445,"y":0.043604651441734532,"c":1,"x":0.093203883552374509},{"h":0.016011012306094474,"w":0.17475728352864583,"c":1,"y":0.093023255901597768,"t":"Questions 14-16","x":0.093203882412640882},{"w":0.36893203735351565,"y":0.12928348930109212,"x":0.093203884344873894,"h":0.019003115264797588,"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","c":1},{"y":0.16551428212225028,"t":"Write the correct letter in boxes 14-16 on your answer sheet.","c":1,"x":0.091184540074683199,"w":0.57684377034505208,"h":0.019223926817516723},{"t":"14 What can we learn from the first paragraph?","h":0.018964155440761243,"c":1,"y":0.20491056283944309,"w":0.46424545288085939,"x":0.089244891971619139},{"w":0.46432851155598953,"x":0.18240590118935415,"t":"where the notion of innate intelligence first began","c":1,"h":0.019946317583600992,"y":0.23340928977237518},{"w":0.58640777587890636,"c":1,"t":"B when ideas about the nature of intelligence began to shift","y":0.25290697662698192,"h":0.017498008038767332,"x":0.13786407325524047},{"y":0.27165109053969472,"x":0.13786407976051332,"t":"C how scientists have responded to changing views of intelligence","c":1,"w":0.65048543294270833,"h":0.017593095607103981},{"w":0.019417475064595541,"c":1,"y":0.29505813935853498,"h":0.01308139551465759,"t":"D","x":0.13980582543580208},{"w":0.63322784423828127,"c":1,"x":0.16690639032925389,"y":0.29049755243616282,"h":0.021227549615307373,"t":"why thinkers turned away from the idea of intelligence being fixed"},{"y":0.32264867066514147,"t":"15 The second paragraph describes how schools encourage students to","h":0.021473211365696798,"c":1,"x":0.093089326291557015,"w":0.6973018900553386},{"c":1,"h":0.01453488311292217,"x":0.13980582557000071,"y":0.35610465134567071,"t":"A","w":0.015533979733785008},{"h":0.01308139551465759,"c":1,"t":"B","x":0.1398058255894182,"y":0.37499999978627585,"w":0.015533979733784981},{"t":"C","h":0.013081395514657479,"c":1,"x":0.13980582552370585,"w":0.017475727399190261,"y":0.39389534866086062},{"y":0.41424418585458989,"w":0.017475727399190288,"h":0.013081395514657479,"c":1,"x":0.1398058255075246,"t":"D"},{"t":"identify their personal ambitions.","y":0.35422625982588241,"x":0.18047184999637855,"h":0.018693512770988518,"w":0.31283126831054686,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.37352024912616111,"w":0.36310679117838546,"t":"help each other to realise their goals.","x":0.17281553650407006,"h":0.016014634485928103},{"w":0.4331647745768229,"y":0.39090055213585784,"c":1,"x":0.18050326887083146,"h":0.018648170162212874,"t":"have confidence in their potential to succeed."},{"h":0.017564116385866968,"y":0.41121495344622216,"t":"concentrate on where their particular strengths lie.","w":0.4796116638183594,"c":1,"x":0.18058251857114735},{"x":0.093101392999808283,"c":1,"w":0.7633537292480469,"h":0.022452164884668169,"y":0.44537953594993673,"t":"16 In the third paragraph, the writer suggests that students with a fixed mindset"},{"c":1,"t":"tend to be less competitive.","w":0.27961163838704428,"h":0.016199376947040545,"y":0.4766355140522649,"x":0.16699029902007007},{"h":0.02148115449233956,"y":0.49280474575799316,"c":1,"t":"B generally have a low sense of self-esteem.","w":0.45082112630208337,"x":0.13961284725387779},{"c":1,"y":0.51598837190110147,"w":0.017475727399190288,"x":0.1398058255075246,"h":0.01308139551465759,"t":"C"},{"h":0.019873862103138351,"y":0.51302967596775195,"c":1,"x":0.17856616887551713,"w":0.58461130777994796,"t":"will only work hard if they are given constant encouragement."},{"t":"D","w":0.017475727399190261,"h":0.01453488311292217,"x":0.13980582552370582,"c":1,"y":0.53343023271679468},{"t":"are afraid to push themselves beyond what they see as their limitations.","w":0.68367986043294271,"h":0.021477522805472327,"x":0.18047967112143395,"y":0.53024868230566646,"c":1},{"w":0.027184467315673824,"t":"90","y":0.96075581381607245,"x":0.095145630322745617,"h":0.01308139551465759,"c":1}],"w":2400,"h":3209}